  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Room of Arches",
    "overview": "The page is her consulting room. A generous sign-wall white carries almost everything; one navy, Azul Aline, signs the name, the headings, the action and the links; photography of her and her real clinic is the protagonist. The arch of the clinic wall is the system's one geometric idea, and it is spent sparingly: it frames her portrait and the facade, it tops the primary action, and it returns as the five thin arcs of her rainbow logo.\n\nDensity is calm and editorial. Sections breathe on a fluid vertical rhythm (up to 9rem), content sits on a 12-column grid that lets photos bleed to the viewport edge while text holds a 62ch measure. Structure is drawn with 1px lines rather than boxes: facts, steps, questions and reviews are separated by hairlines, never enclosed in cards. Colour is restrained to the point of rarity; the logo pastels never fill a surface.\n\nThe world refuses the category default of a split hero with pills, card grids and pastel everywhere (direction contract, confirmed by the user).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White wall ground, one strong navy, graphite ink.",
      "Arch geometry: portrait and facade frames, arch-topped actions, the logo arcs.",
      "Lines instead of containers; no cards.",
      "Serif display in navy at large sizes; plain humanist sans for everything read.",
      "Motion is slow and settling (one expo-out curve), never bouncy."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Strong Colour Rule",
        "body": "Azul Aline is the only saturated colour on any screen. A second accent never appears; emphasis comes from size and the serif, not from another hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Thin Rainbow Rule",
        "body": "The logo pastels exist only as stroked arcs (2-5px). They never fill a block, a button, a background or a card.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Serif Speaks For Her Rule",
        "body": "Young Serif is reserved for her name, section titles, step titles, quotes and her answers. Anything a parent scans for logistics (facts, labels, buttons, navigation on desktop) is Figtree.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "No uppercase, no tracked-out labels anywhere in the build. Hierarchy comes from size, face and colour.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lines Not Boxes Rule",
        "body": "Group content with a 1px top rule (Hairline on light, translucent white or lilac on navy), never with a bordered or shadowed card.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Arches Rule",
        "body": "The full arch frame belongs to the hero portrait and the facade. Other photos are soft rectangles; adding a third arch frame dilutes the signature.",
